.TH SWIFTJ2K 1 "September 22, 2026" "12.1.0-dev.3" "Swift Image Compression Suite"
.SH NAME
swiftj2k \- help, version and capability reporting for SwiftJ2K
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B swiftj2k
.RI [ options ] " command " [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
This development tool provides help, version and truthful library capability
reporting.
The library implements scalar lossless JPEG 2000 Part 1 coding for unsigned
greyscale images; the reserved encode, decode, inspect and validate commands
and native transcode are not yet wired to it and return 4 without opening
input, consuming standard input or creating output.
Build with Swift 6.2 or later (6.4 qualified) in Swift 6 language mode. Apple OS
minimum is 26.0.
CLI hosts are macOS and Linux; consult qualification records for executed
coverage.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B capabilities [\-\-json]
Report actual library encode/decode/inspect support. JSON is one document on
stdout.
True values describe the library API, not the reserved CLI commands.
.TP
.B help [command]
Show global or command-specific help. No arguments also show global help.
.TP
.B version
Show the development version.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help, including after a command.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the development version.
.TP
.B \-v, \-vv, \-vvv, \-vvvv, \-vvvvv
Increase diagnostic verbosity, up to 5.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose LEVEL, \-\-verbose=LEVEL
Set level to 1 through 5, or + through +++++. Bare verbose increments once.
.TP
.B \-verbose: LEVEL, \-verbose:LEVEL
Equivalent explicit verbosity spelling; bare \-verbose increments once.
.TP
.B \-q, \-\-quiet
Suppress optional diagnostics; errors remain visible. Conflicts with
verbosity.
.SH DIAGNOSTIC LEVELS
Default 0 reports errors only. Levels are cumulative:
1 summary; 2 stages; 3 capability/configuration details; 4 elapsed timing;
5 bounded trace. Invalid levels or totals above 5 return 2.
Explicit levels set and repeated flags increment in argument order.
Diagnostics use stderr. Requested help/version/capability data uses stdout.
No payload bytes, metadata, raw addresses or input/output paths are logged.
.SH RESERVED CODEC SYNTAX
Codec command help lists reserved \-i/\-\-input, \-o/\-\-output,
\-\-input-format, \-\-output-format, \-\-mode, \-\-max-error,
\-\-backend, \-\-copy-policy, \-\-threads, \-\-max-memory,
\-\-timeout, \-\-overwrite and \-\-json.
These are not implemented payload operations. A single hyphen will denote
standard
input/output in a future codec command. Default future mode is lossless and
copy
policy is require-sharing. No private intermediate image format is
implemented.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success/help/version; 2 invalid usage; 4 unsupported operation;
6 output I/O failure including a closed pipe.
Future codec statuses reserve 3 malformed input, 5 resource/deadline,
7 internal failure and 130 user cancellation.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
swiftj2k \-h
swiftj2k help capabilities
swiftj2k capabilities \-\-json \-vv
swiftj2k capabilities \-verbose: 3
swiftj2k capabilities \-\-verbose=+++++
.fi
.SH INSTALLATION
Scripts/install-cli.sh installs or updates the executable and this page
together.
Use \-\-prefix for an absolute prefix (default /usr/local), \-\-destdir or
DESTDIR
for staging, and \-\-binary for a prebuilt binary matching VERSION.
Files are PREFIX/bin/swiftj2k and PREFIX/share/man/man1/swiftj2k.1.
For custom prefixes use man \-M PREFIX/share/man swiftj2k, or configure
MANPATH.
No index refresh is needed for direct lookup; no sudo runs automatically.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR man (1)
.PP
CLI.md and Documentation/Engineering/OS27CLI/README.md in the SwiftJ2K
repository.
